<!--
	Oracles: the Prophet line (Prophet, Hierophant). Buff templates, buff shops, the scheme
	buffer and the buff books teach every buff, so the Prophet line no longer buffs: it fights
	in the future tense. See README "Oracles and Totem Warchiefs" and
	config/Custom/OraclesWarchiefs.ini. The retail buffs are out of their class trees.

	27530-27540  Oracle skills, learned from the Grand Masters like any class skill.

	PROPHECIES (the Prophecy effect, model/actor/holders/player/Prophecies.java): a prophecy does
	nothing when it lands. When its time runs out it comes true; if it is cancelled or its
	target dies first, it fizzles. A prophecy that comes true gives the Oracle a Foresight
	(27537, up to 5). The prophecies on enemies are debuffs that roll to land like any debuff.
	  27530 Prophecy of Doom       enemy, 5 s: 27531 Doom Strike (holy magic damage), x1.5 if
	                               the target is still within 300 of where it stood.
	  27532 Prophecy of Salvation  ally, 6 s: heals back the damage taken while it was on.
	  27533 Prophecy of Ruin       enemy, 5 s: 27534 stun if the target cast a skill meanwhile,
	                               else 27535 silence.
	  27536 Prophecy of Reversal   ally, 6 s: HP, MP, CP and place are written down when it
	                               lands; the ally comes back to them (never lower than it is).
	  27538 Fulfilment             Hierophant, needs 5 Foresight: every prophecy of the Oracle
	                               comes true now, x1.5 (no Foresight from these).
	  27539 Glimpse                Hierophant toggle: Evasion +4, a hit taking 30% of the
	                               Oracle's HP makes it step back 300 (once a minute).
	  27540 Unwritten              Hierophant finale: Doom on every enemy and Salvation on every
	                               party member within 600 (5 minute reuse).

	Keep custom skill ids below 32768. The client needs Skillname-e.dat / Skillgrp.dat rows for
	every id here (client/OraclesWarchiefs). The icons are those of the retired buffs.
-->
